WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.566
Hi, good morning, Ziad.

00:00:01.566 --> 00:00:03.199
Hope you got some sleep.

00:00:03.199 --> 00:00:05.922
Today's Saturday, November twenty-first.

00:00:05.922 --> 00:00:11.367
One hard run on the calendar, then a dry, mild day that's pretty much all yours.

00:00:11.367 --> 00:00:13.886
Here's one to chew on while you move.

00:00:13.886 --> 00:00:19.603
Why should an M.P.3 always be made from the raw audio, and never from another M.P.3?

00:00:19.603 --> 00:00:20.965
Answer's at the end.

00:00:20.965 --> 00:00:24.164
Weather's easy today, dry and on the mild side.

00:00:24.164 --> 00:00:26.478
Tomorrow's the one to plan around.

00:00:26.478 --> 00:00:41.385
A coastal storm rolls in Sunday afternoon and runs into early Monday, anywhere from half an inch to a couple of inches of rain depending on its track, with gusts near thirty Sunday night, and it turns much colder after.

00:00:41.385 --> 00:00:44.788
I couldn't get today's exact high or wind numbers.

00:00:44.788 --> 00:00:45.741
Okay, the day.

00:00:45.741 --> 00:00:50.234
Calendar has five by four intervals at seven, about fifty minutes.

00:00:50.234 --> 00:00:52.684
After that, nothing on there at all.

00:00:52.684 --> 00:01:00.036
And that painting show on Starr Street from Wednesday's memo opens today, if you want a slow stop somewhere.

00:01:00.036 --> 00:01:00.989
Alright, news.

00:01:00.989 --> 00:01:02.010
Just two today.

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:05.209
A big ruling from the World Court in The Hague.

00:01:05.209 --> 00:01:15.691
The judges found, nine to six, that Myanmar committed genocide against the Rohingya, the Muslim minority that was driven out by the hundreds of thousands.

00:01:15.691 --> 00:01:20.796
Britain responded by ordering Myanmar's defense attaché out of the country.

00:01:20.796 --> 00:01:23.791
Myanmar's government brushed the ruling off.

00:01:23.791 --> 00:01:26.378
And one that ties back to all the A.I.

00:01:26.378 --> 00:01:26.990
building.

00:01:26.990 --> 00:01:33.593
The Senate passed a permitting bill, sixty-two to thirty-three, with fourteen Democrats on board.

00:01:33.593 --> 00:01:39.651
It shortens how long lawsuits can hold up projects and narrows the environmental reviews.

00:01:39.651 --> 00:01:45.437
The point is to speed up new power plants and data centers, including on public land.

00:01:45.437 --> 00:01:49.861
It goes to the House next, with a vote maybe the week after next.

00:01:49.861 --> 00:01:52.924
Okay, here's the main thing for next weekend.

00:01:52.924 --> 00:02:02.249
Sunday the twenty-ninth, Starr Bar, on Starr Street in Bushwick, has a night called Conversations with Filmmakers in its back stage room.

00:02:02.249 --> 00:02:05.040
It looks like it runs about six to eight.

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:11.302
It's a few short films by underground New York filmmakers, then a Q and A, then hanging out.

00:02:11.302 --> 00:02:16.952
Twenty bucks, twenty-one and up, and the money goes toward finishing an indie film.

00:02:16.952 --> 00:02:21.989
It's small, it's local, and the people who made the stuff are right there.

00:02:21.989 --> 00:02:28.183
That's a good room for someone who shoots, because you can just ask how they lit something.

00:02:28.183 --> 00:02:30.566
Today's challenge is for your body.

00:02:30.566 --> 00:02:35.739
Tonight, after the intervals, find a stair edge and do ten slow calf raises.

00:02:35.739 --> 00:02:41.456
Up in one second, then take a full three seconds to lower your heels below the step.

00:02:41.456 --> 00:02:42.205
Two rounds.

00:02:42.205 --> 00:02:45.064
The slow lowering is the part that counts.

00:02:45.064 --> 00:02:53.777
It's the cheapest insurance there is for your Achilles and calves, the parts that take the most from running and pushing pedals.

00:02:53.777 --> 00:02:56.295
Okay, something you've been learning.

00:02:56.295 --> 00:02:59.698
Remember pricing out that shared car with friends?

00:02:59.698 --> 00:03:02.625
Here's what a lease is really charging you.

00:03:02.625 --> 00:03:04.259
Start with depreciation.

00:03:04.259 --> 00:03:07.594
A new car loses value fastest right at the start.

00:03:07.594 --> 00:03:13.584
Often something like a fifth in the first year, and around half within about five years.

00:03:13.584 --> 00:03:15.899
After that the curve flattens out.

00:03:15.899 --> 00:03:21.344
So whoever owns a car in its first few years eats the steepest part of the drop.

00:03:21.344 --> 00:03:23.999
A lease is basically renting that drop.

00:03:23.999 --> 00:03:29.036
When you lease, the dealer predicts what the car will be worth at the end.

00:03:29.036 --> 00:03:31.282
That's called the residual value.

00:03:31.282 --> 00:03:38.021
Say it's a thirty thousand dollar car, and they expect it to be worth about half after three years.

00:03:38.021 --> 00:03:43.738
Your payments mostly cover the fifteen thousand in between, split across the months.

00:03:43.738 --> 00:03:46.053
Then there's the part people miss.

00:03:46.053 --> 00:03:52.519
You're also paying to borrow, and on a lease it hides in a tiny number called the money factor.

00:03:52.519 --> 00:03:55.854
Something like zero point zero zero one two five.

00:03:55.854 --> 00:03:57.352
It looks like nothing.

00:03:57.352 --> 00:03:58.509
Here's the trick.

00:03:58.509 --> 00:04:02.933
Multiply it by twenty-four hundred and you get the interest rate.

00:04:02.933 --> 00:04:05.384
That one comes out to three percent.

00:04:05.384 --> 00:04:10.080
Dealers can nudge that number up, and most people never think to ask.

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:12.259
There's a quirk in the math too.

00:04:12.259 --> 00:04:18.112
The interest part gets charged on the starting price plus the residual added together.

00:04:18.112 --> 00:04:24.375
So a car that holds its value well, with a high residual, can still cost a lot to borrow on.

00:04:24.375 --> 00:04:26.621
So the honest comparison is this.

00:04:26.621 --> 00:04:31.862
Leasing new means paying for the steepest years of the curve, plus that rate.

00:04:31.862 --> 00:04:38.737
Buying a car that's two or three years old means someone else already paid for the worst of the drop.

00:04:38.737 --> 00:04:42.889
You just have to own the repairs that come with an older car.

00:04:42.889 --> 00:04:46.905
So: calendar says intervals at seven, then a free Saturday.

00:04:46.905 --> 00:04:49.219
Do those slow calf raises tonight.

00:04:49.219 --> 00:04:56.162
The answer: every pass makes new guesses on top of the last one's damage, so it smears more each time.

00:04:56.162 --> 00:04:58.000
Have a good Saturday, Ziad.
